<section id="faq" class="ns-section ns-faq" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
  <div class="ns-container ns-editorial-grid">
    <header class="ns-section-heading">
      <h2 id="faq-title" class="t-heading">Questions</h2>
    </header>
    <div class="ns-faq__items">
      <details>
        <summary>Is our data sent anywhere?</summary>
        <p>Yes. When the agent uses the AI model, the text it is working on is sent to the model provider. Everything else, such as the agent's files, settings and history, is stored under accounts in your name.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Do we need technical staff?</summary>
        <p>Not for a pilot, which runs on the vendor's hosted service. A server you own needs someone to keep it updated and backed up, either my ongoing support or someone else.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>What if the agent gets something wrong?</summary>
        <p>It drafts, and a person approves what goes out. Every run is logged, and we agree the acceptance test before work starts.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>What if we stop working with you?</summary>
        <p>The accounts, keys, configuration and notes are in your name, and the agent keeps running.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Who owns the work when it is done?</summary>
        <p>You do, once the final invoice is paid: the configuration, prompts, code, and notes produced for you. The vendor's terms still apply to their service. I don't keep a right to your documents.</p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
